Title: Wrong Table
Author: Script Glow

INT. CORNER CAFE - DAY

Midmorning bustle. CLAIRE, forties, sharp blazer, laptop open, checks her watch. BEN, thirties, holding a single sunflower, approaches her table.

BEN
Claire?

CLAIRE
You must be Ben. Right on time. Sit, please.

BEN
This is for you. It's one flower. The shop was out of the others.

CLAIRE
That's thoughtful. Nobody has ever brought me a flower to one of these.

BEN
Really? That's a crime. So, have you done a lot of these?

CLAIRE
Four this week.

BEN
Four! Wow. You're busy.

CLAIRE
We're growing fast. I like to meet everyone in person before I decide.

BEN
Smart. You can't tell anything from a profile.

CLAIRE
Exactly. On paper you look very strong.

BEN
(pleased)
Thank you. I worked hard on the photos.

CLAIRE
The photos?

BEN
My sister took them. At the beach.

CLAIRE
I didn't see any photos. I saw your resume.

BEN
My what?

CLAIRE
Your resume. For the operations manager position.

A long beat.

BEN
You're not Claire from the app.

CLAIRE
I am Claire from Hollister Freight. Who is Claire from the app?

They both look across the cafe. A woman by the window gives a small, uncertain wave.

BEN
Oh no.

CLAIRE
Are you Ben Alvarez?

BEN
I'm Ben Foster.

CLAIRE
So my candidate is late.

BEN
And my date has been watching me give you a sunflower.

CLAIRE
For what it's worth, you're doing better than most of my candidates.

BEN
Really?

CLAIRE
You showed up early, you made eye contact, and you brought a gift. That's more than I got all week.

BEN
Do you need operations experience for the job?

CLAIRE
Do you have any operations experience?

BEN
I'm organizing my sister's wedding. Two hundred guests, three caterers, one budget, zero cooperation.

CLAIRE
(interested despite herself)
How's it going?

BEN
On time and under budget.

CLAIRE
Huh.

BEN
I'm a very good logistics person. I'm a terrible date person. Clearly.

CLAIRE
Go say hello to her. She's still waiting.

BEN
Right. Yes. Of course.

He stands, then turns back.

BEN
Can I have the flower back?

CLAIRE
No. Send me your resume.

BEN
Seriously?

CLAIRE
Seriously. And Ben? Tell the other Claire you're great with logistics. Everybody loves a plan.

He goes. She smells the sunflower, smiles, and turns back to her laptop.
